- **Sign extension is the big one.** [38;5;10mprintHexCharLine[0m takes a [38;5;10mchar[0m, which is promoted to [38;5;10mint[0m through the variadic call, and [38;5;10m%x[0m then reinterprets that [38;5;10mint[0m as [38;5;10munsigned[0m. Because [38;5;10mchar[0m is signed on x86-64 Linux, any result byte ≥ 0x80 prints as 8 hex digits: input [38;5;10m0x7f[0m → [38;5;10mffffff80[0m, [38;5;10m0xfe[0m → [38;5;10mffffffff[0m. The [38;5;10m%02x[0m width of 2 is only a [3mminimum[23m, so it never truncates. I modeled this as an explicit [38;5;10mi8 → i32 → u32[0m chain.[0m[0m
